{
  "name": "Control Rate",
  "description": "Two signal rates in one patch. Pixel-rate cables (circles) are GLSL evaluated per pixel; control-rate cables (diamonds, dashed) run once per frame in JavaScript, keep state and reach the shader as live uniforms. An LFO through a Lag tints the glowing cell edges, a Beat Divider steps a Counter through four palettes (Select + Lag glide), an Envelope Follower on the bass (or the beat) punches the zoom, and a Threshold -> Trigger -> Sample & Hold of a random value shifts the hue. Play music or the metronome to drive it.",
  "version": "1.0",
  "timestamp": "2026-10-25T13:04:19.290Z",
  "graph": {
    "nodes": [
      {
        "id": 0,
        "type": "Comment",
        "x": 40,
        "y": 30,
        "data": {
          "text": "# Control rate\nTwo kinds of cables. **Pixel rate** (circles, solid): GLSL, evaluated for every pixel, no memory. **Control rate** (diamonds, dashed): JavaScript, once per frame before rendering, can keep state; reaches the shader as a live uniform (never recompiles). Events are dotted with a bolt.\n- LFO -> Lag -> glow colour\n- Beat Divider -> Counter -> palette index (Select + Lag glide)\n- Envelope Follower on the bass -> zoom punch\n- Threshold -> Trigger -> Sample & Hold of a random value -> hue\nPlay music or the metronome (top bar) to drive the zoom.",
          "width": 520,
          "height": 230,
          "color": "violet"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
